{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"jarl/proofs/engine/README.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-04T15:26:23.933210Z","id":"0f61efb11f417340779c4ce9db2aa67e618d5b6f179c0562c7d2df064a09449e","body":{"detail":"jarl/proofs/engine/Engine/Cluster.lean (Cluster.persist) sets the durable state to the node's whole State when Ready::persisted runs. A real host persists State::write's delta (entries, truncation, snapshot, hard state); the storage-view project proves that delta equivalent to the checkpoint only under explicit premises, and that composition is not part of the M3 theorems.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":68},"end":{"line":70},"content_hash":"9c14befc521b1550129db86cf85e2eaa2f0e5069356ef6f3446070100a39a6f2"},"suggested_fix":"Model the durable state as the result of applying Write to the previous durable state, and import storage-view's checkpoint equivalence (or reprove it on the typed translation) to discharge the step.","summary":"M3 persistence is modelled as writing the whole node state, not the Write delta a host applies","tags":["session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"jarl/proofs/engine/README.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-04T15:26:23.933281Z","id":"15c35ddd23ac62d855fb81f310b32312d70724546c644144cad85e6529577a85","body":{"detail":"raft_snapshot_safety (jarl/proofs/engine/Engine/Main.lean) shows that an exposed snapshot's last LogId agrees with committed history. The ghost history does not track which application state a snapshot carries, so a compact call with a value unrelated to the committed prefix is not ruled out; CORRECTNESS_PLAN S10 asks for the application interpretation at the boundary as well.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":71},"end":{"line":72},"content_hash":"9e75b58f190c3611ce81ad94fc5d53676b3fbf48d20794c7da388892dc01b995"},"suggested_fix":"Add an abstract application function to the ghost (state after applying a committed prefix), require compact's value to equal it as a host precondition, and carry it through Install messages and restore.","summary":"Snapshot safety covers the boundary identity but not the snapshot's application state","tags":["session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"jarl/proofs/engine/README.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-04T15:26:23.933302Z","id":"13d3acc72c3edb0722598e13645d811d600c63615a0553ebbfb7ae68d8361465","body":{"detail":"jarl/proofs/engine/project.json roots are the fixed Node operations. Membership changes, learners, joint configurations and pre-vote probes (CORRECTNESS_PLAN M4, S11-S14) are untranslated or unproved, and Engine/Main.lean's Assumptions fix one shared membership.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":73},"end":{"line":73},"content_hash":"cdd9bca6ba036aad1f2a53cc1c114082a58bf0a6a98d3e25cfb60fd324458b2d"},"suggested_fix":"M4: extend the ghost history with configuration lineage and reuse the M3 invariant architecture for the dynamic engine.","summary":"M3 covers only the fixed engine; the dynamic Cluster engine has no global safety proof on the typed translation","tags":["session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
